    "created_at": "2020-06-07T15:30:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-07T15:30:06Z",
    "body": "- `task +DUETODAY` – list tasks that are due today \r\n- `task +WEEK` – list tasks that are due this week \r\n- `task +WEEK count` – show number of tasks that are due this week\r\n- `task +OVERDUE` – list tasks that are overdue  \r\n\r\nhttps://taskwarrior.org/docs/tags.html\r\nhttps://taskwarrior.org/docs/filter.html\r\nThose are filters which return a non-zero status if they are empty.\r\n\r\n```\r\nfor task in (task +ACTIVE _uuids)\r\n      task _get $task.description\r\n  end\r\n```\r\nget the decription of all the tasks that have been started.\r\nhttps://taskwarrior.org/docs/dom.html\r\n\r\nI think it would be useful to show different symbols for e.g.:\r\n- no tasks due today\r\n- tasks due this week\r\n- tasks due today\r\n- tasks overdue\r\n\r\nand maybe also: name of the active (started) task that is due next.\r\n\r\nFor me it would make sense to show these in the right prompt, not the left.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
