    "created_at": "2024-09-15T11:28:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-09-15T11:30:32Z",
    "body": "I'd like to share an alternate (additional) approach to provide an easier Starship<->TaskWarrior integration, as I'm thinking on tackling it myself and just in case anyone else finds it useful or helps refine current ideas (and hopefully, get what I bet will be very useful feedback):\r\nSo far, and quite understandably, the burden of configuring the Starship's output falls on Starship's side. It is very customizable and very capable. I'm very happy with it and I can't remember anything i couldn't achieve with it, so far.\r\n\r\nThe alternate option (in addition to the current one) would be to shift the output configuration to TaskWarrior's side.\r\nIt would require creating an additional Starship `taskwarrior-easy` module, which would always run some `taskwarrior starship` kind of command and just output the result, thus moving configuration logic to TW's config.\r\n\r\nI'm not such an advanced TW user yet, but my guess is that by the very nature of TW, users are already quite capable of building complex logic and workflows on the TW side. This way, they can build on their existing knowledge and configuration work and avoid the complexity on Starship's side (less support requests, anyone? :smiley:). With so many TW options and commands, Starship's config might become quite messy, in the long run.\r\nWDYT? Feedback is much appreciated.\r\nJust my 2c.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
